{#
    WHERE A PERSON LANDS AFTER SIGNING OUT. SimpleSAMLphp has no logout PAGE as
    such: an IdP-initiated single logout ends at `/module.php/core/welcome`, which
    is this template. Stock, it reads "This is the front page of the SimpleSAMLphp
    authentication software" and points at the SimpleSAMLphp documentation — true
    of the software, useless to a faculty member who has just signed out of a
    practice CWL, and it drops them out of the UBC look at the same time.

    So this is themed AND rewritten. It says what happened, and it says again what
    this IdP is, because somebody who arrives here out of context has no other clue.
#}
{% set pagetitle = 'Signed out'|trans %}
{% extends "@core/_layout.twig" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="container">
    <div class="row-fluid">
        <div class="span12">
            <h1>You are signed out</h1>
            <p>
                Your session with this <strong>practice</strong> sign-in service has ended.
                Any application you signed in to through it has been told to sign you out too.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row-fluid">
        <div class="span8">
            <div class="well">
                <h4>This is not real CWL</h4>
                <p>
                    This service exists so that an application can be built and demonstrated
                    against a CWL-shaped sign-in <em>before</em> it has real CWL approvals. The
                    accounts it knows are test accounts. Nothing you do here affects a real UBC
                    account, and a real CWL password should never be typed into it.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
